statement:
Let n, l >= 0, U any set, and V a contract rectifiable n-varifold in U with weight mu such that y -> p_y := V.tangentProj y is mu-a.e. strongly measurable. Let q be a linear isometry of R^(n+l), u : R^n -> R^l continuous on a set Omega in R^n, F(x) := q(graphPoint(x, u x)), Du(x) := fderiv u x, and for linear A let P_A be the orthogonal projection onto q(span{graphPoint(v, A v)}). Assume:
(E1) for every Borel A contained in Omega and every Borel g : R^(n+l) -> [0, infinity], the lower integral over A of g(F(x)) dx is at most the lower integral over F(A) of g d mu;
(E2) p_{F(x)} = P_{Du(x)} for Lebesgue-a.e. x in Omega.
Let S be a linear subspace, z in R^n, r real and s > 0 such that:
- the closed ball B_r(z) is contained in Omega;
- hsNorm(Du(x)) <= 1/4 and |F(x) - F(z)| <= s for all x in B_r(z);
- P_{Du(z)} = S.starProjection;
- mu(B_s(F(z))) < infinity.
Then the lower integral over B_r(z) of ofReal(hsNormSq(Du(x) - Du(z))) dx is at most ofReal(s^n V.tiltExcess (F(z)) s S).
